{
  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_032 (multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, concat) achieved the best accuracy so far (0.688), a ~3.5 pt gain over the best RNA-only model (config_006, 0.653). However, image-only resnet50 scored only 0.208, raising uncertainty about whether the image branch is contributing meaningful complementary signal or whether the modest multimodal gain is partly noise. Question: config_038 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings identical to config_032. This isolates the effect of image representation quality. If imagenet_vit_l yields a substantial further improvement, it confirms the image modality carries extractable signal and justifies further investment in the image branch; if it yields little or no gain, it suggests the image modality contributes minimally regardless of encoder strength, and the small gain in config_032 may be within noise. Why best next: it is a clean single-variable extension of the current best configuration, directly tests a critical design question (is the image branch worth keeping and investing in), and avoids the lower-priority question of fusion method (concat vs. weighted) which is less informative if the image signal itself is weak."
}

